A line over the 1,000-byte display cap is shown cut and named, rather than pushing the answer
over `--max-bytes` into a refusal. The second call is the control: 900 bytes is shown whole.

```console
$ lets show long.js --max-bytes 2000
── long.js  (1-1 of 1)
1 	…
── showed 1 target · 1 line · 1 long line cut

$ lets show short.js --max-bytes 2000
── short.js  (1-1 of 1)
1 	
── showed 1 target · 1 line

```
